// Adaptive Sorting Algorithm Implementation
// This program implements a sorting algorithm that can be evolved to adapt to different data patterns

use std::cmp::Ordering;

// EVOLVE-BLOCK-START
// HYPOTHESIS-1: Hybrid introsort with median-of-three pivot and insertion sort cutoff will improve performance on all input patterns
// MECHANISM-1: Median-of-three avoids worst-case O(n^2) on sorted data; insertion sort is fast for small subarrays; depth limit prevents degenerate recursion
// EXPECT-1: performance_score > 0.985
// RESULT-1: CONFIRMED (actual=0.9981475628917184)
// HYPOTHESIS-2: Simplifying code by removing unused is_nearly_sorted reduces code length while maintaining adaptability
// MECHANISM-2: Fewer unused functions means cleaner code; the hybrid approach inherently adapts to data patterns without explicit detection
// EXPECT-2: combined_score > 0.99
